<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="11">
<name>Control System</name>
<section id="1001O_S001F" variety="S001F">
<name>Cruise Control</name>
<ttl id="1001O_S001F_74QXD_T00FC" variety="T00FC">
<name>Radar Cruise Control System</name>
<para id="RM00000064Q00CX" category="C" type-id="303W4" name-id="5915B-00" from="200708">
<dtccode>U1102/72</dtccode>
<dtcname>Distance Control → Radar Communication Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000064Q00CX_02" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBC00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The distance control computer assembly sends vehicle speed and estimated curve information to the millimeter wave radar sensor assembly. The radar sensor sends information such as the presence of a preceding vehicle, vehicle-to-vehicle distance and relative speed to the distance control computer assembly. The distance control computer assembly sends this information to the engine control computer to perform cruise control.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="left">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.97in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.11in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Diagnosis Description</ptxt>
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Diagnosis Condition</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Abnormal Condition</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>U1102/72</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Control vehicle speed (40 - 100 km/h), cruise control main switch ON (vehicle-to-vehicle distance control mode)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Communication data from the distance control computer assembly to the millimeter wave radar sensor assembly is abnormal</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Distance Control Computer Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wire harness and connector (millimeter wave radar sensor assembly - distance control computer assembly)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Millimeter Wave Radar Sensor Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000064Q00CX_03" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBD00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B179588J01" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000064Q00CX_04" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBE00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When the distance control computer assembly is replaced with a new one, be sure to perform initialization. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002GO2003X"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When the millimeter wave radar sensor assembly is replaced with a new one, be sure to perform radar axis adjustment. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM0000028Z6003X"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>A poor connector connection is a possible cause of this DTC, so make sure that each connector is securely connected.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000064Q00CX_05" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0016" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBF00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Distance Control Computer Assembly - Millimeter Wave Radar Sensor)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D702RX"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the millimeter wave radar sensor assembly and distance control computer assembly connectors.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the connector terminals of the vehicle wire harness. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM00000064800HX"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E143508J02" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.47in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC1" colwidth="0.81in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.85in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>4(LRRD) - 23(LRRD)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>5(IGB) - 13(IGB)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.46in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.80in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="0.87in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>23 (LRRD) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>13 (IGB) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of the vehicle side harness connector of the millimeter wave radar sensor assembly.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.47in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC3" colwidth="0.84in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.82in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>2 (SGND) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of the vehicle side harness connector of the distance control computer assembly.</ptxt>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COLSPEC4" colwidth="2.47in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC5" colwidth="0.84in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC6" colwidth="0.82in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10 (SGND) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0021" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0019" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0021" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBH00000">
<testtitle>Replace Distance Control Computer Assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Replace the distance control computer assembly with a new one. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000028Z2003X"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform initialization of the radar cruise control. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000002GO2003X"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0023" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0023" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CIB00000">
<testtitle>Clear DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), clear the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000064C00EX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0017" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0017" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBG00000">
<testtitle>Check DTCs (Radar Cruise Control System)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Put the vehicle in the conditions under which the DTC is detected.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>The system cannot detect the malfunction unless the detection conditions are met.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<test2>
<ptxt>Drive within the cruise control set vehicle speed range.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Turn the cruise control main switch ON and put the system in vehicle-to-vehicle distance control mode standby.</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), check the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000064C00EX"/>)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.89in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.24in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC U1102 is not output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC U1102 is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0022" fin="true">A</down>
<right ref="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0007" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0022">
<testtitle>Complete</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0019">
<testtitle>Repair or Replace Wire Harness or Connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000064Q00CX_05_0007">
<testtitle>Replace Millimeter Wave Radar Sensor Assembly<xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000028Z9003X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
